# Barn owl

The barn owl is a pale, long-winged nocturnal predator found on every continent
except Antarctica. It is abroad between dusk and dawn, quartering rough pasture
at walking pace and dropping onto voles and mice that it locates in complete
darkness by ear alone. The facial disc funnels sound toward asymmetric ear
openings, and the fringed leading edge of the wing breaks up the airflow so the
approach is inaudible to prey and to a listener alike. By day it sleeps in a
hollow tree, a ruin or a church tower. See [[tytonidae]] and [[strigiformes]].
